\paragraph{CausalForest.}
Theorem~\ref{thm:bias_identity} characterizes bias for any estimator whose inputs pass through a confusion matrix; CausalForest~\cite{wager2018causal} with a noisy effect modifier $\hat{Z}$ inherits the same $M_{\text{global}}^{-1} M_s$ structure because the forest's splitting variable is contaminated identically.
With CausalForest ($K{=}4$, extreme, $n{=}500$), EC-HTE reduces $|\text{bias}|$ from 0.191 to 0.039 (4.9$\times$) with coverage 0.90; global amplifies bias up to 5.9$\times$ (Table~\ref{tab:main_results}; bootstrap SE in Appendix~\ref{app:bootstrap_se}).

